WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:07.400
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:12.967
Y'know, if I had some Pop-Tarts
right now, I wouldn't just eat them;

00:00:12.967 --> 00:00:16.347
I'd make some sort of hexagonal
structure out of them, THEN eat them.

00:00:16.347 --> 00:00:17.534
Pop-Tarts Center.

00:00:17.534 --> 00:00:20.667
Why is this locked? It's a ladder.

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:23.467
The mesh is so big, I could grab on anyway.

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:25.592
I just don't get the point of this.

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:27.567
It must be some insurance thing.

00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:32.100
Yeah, the world ended. I guess paying for
insurance on anything was a complete waste.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.033
But I don't have any money now, either.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.533
I guess I should've just
spent it all on tattoos.

00:00:36.533 --> 00:00:38.333
You can take THAT with you.

00:00:38.333 --> 00:00:39.067
[hocks]

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:42.067
Wait, no. I don't know when
I'm going to drink again.

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:44.733
I have to protect my precious bodily fluids.

00:00:44.733 --> 00:00:47.433
Huh. I don't hear any gunshots.

00:00:47.433 --> 00:00:50.467
That's actually exactly
what I don't want to hear.

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:55.633
I mean, I'm not hearing an attack chopper,
and that's kind of all that matters anymore.

00:00:55.633 --> 00:01:00.602
Oh my God! It's actually
quiet! This is so nice!

00:01:00.602 --> 00:01:03.400
What a great night to not be dead!

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:08.233
I mean, a great night for me. It's a
really bad night for a lot of people.

00:01:08.233 --> 00:01:10.667
Yeah, I met a lot of dead people today.

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:15.200
If civilization ever gets back on its
feet, I'm going to have so many interviews,

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.467
since I'll have met a lot of
historically-significant dead people.

00:01:18.467 --> 00:01:24.000
Not a chopper in sight and buildings
I can duck into--this is amazing!

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.333
Oh, okay. Yeah.

00:01:26.333 --> 00:01:28.633
Good! I would be a little
nervous at this point

00:01:28.633 --> 00:01:31.767
if there wasn't some horrendous
problem everywhere I went.

00:01:31.767 --> 00:01:34.267
Oh. Okay, that's...weird.

00:01:34.267 --> 00:01:36.367
Oh yeah, that's a lot of blood.

00:01:36.367 --> 00:01:37.933
This is murder alley.

00:01:37.933 --> 00:01:41.533
Oh wow. They put cardboard over the
blood so they could walk over it.

00:01:41.533 --> 00:01:43.597
That is some cynical shi...

00:01:43.597 --> 00:01:46.667
Oh, so this really IS murder
alley. It doesn't go anywhere;

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:49.200
it's JUST for killing people. All right!

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.967
I guess architecture reflects
the needs of the times.

00:01:51.967 --> 00:01:54.090
I'm still not sure what happened at the base;

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.233
there were so many holes,
it could've been anything--

00:01:56.233 --> 00:02:01.233
the aliens signaling, the mole--it
could've just been them tracking me.

00:02:01.233 --> 00:02:02.918
What the hell is this?

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:07.733
No... No! I wasn't addressing
you! I was talking to myself!

00:02:07.733 --> 00:02:09.300
Sorry about the confusion!

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:10.700
[multiple crows calling]

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:12.533
A lot of birds...

00:02:12.533 --> 00:02:14.067
Caw!

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:15.233
Well, that's that.

00:02:15.233 --> 00:02:19.079
What the hell is this? Did they
tie the rope to his hip bone?

00:02:19.079 --> 00:02:20.233
Why?

00:02:20.233 --> 00:02:22.133
What's the message here?

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:24.800
Make like a tree and get out of here?

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:27.167
Y'know, I thought I would
adapt better to the future,

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:31.300
but I really am lost on a
lot of the cultural contexts.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:32.033
Or maybe it's not--

00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:34.000
[bird flapping]
Jesus Christ!

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.067
Well, I'm adapting better than that guy!

00:02:36.067 --> 00:02:37.967
So that means the context doesn't matter!

00:02:37.967 --> 00:02:40.200
I'm right! I should never forget that!

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.533
If I was in charge, this
wouldn't be happening.

00:02:42.533 --> 00:02:46.167
Yeah, today has been
frustrating, because I saw a lot.

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:48.567
And what is THIS?!

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:52.600
Okay! I see what happened, but...how?

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.533
Is there a machine that launches these?

00:02:55.533 --> 00:02:57.200
I don't see one.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:00.567
So somebody was just tossing these
with work gloves or something?

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:05.638
These are big! That probably took
both hands! Ultimate-ULTIMATE Frisbee.

00:03:06.522 --> 00:03:10.467
Yeah, they're stuck in the wall.
This wasn't his first throw.

00:03:10.467 --> 00:03:11.533
How'd he do that?

00:03:11.533 --> 00:03:12.333
[zombie growls]

00:03:12.333 --> 00:03:12.900
Dammit...

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:21.267
Okay, there's a story here, though
I think I missed the exciting part.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.433
Looks kind of Shakespearean.

00:03:23.433 --> 00:03:23.933
Hup.

00:03:26.967 --> 00:03:28.033
No monologues!

00:03:29.633 --> 00:03:32.100
Well, someone's not getting their inheritance.

00:03:32.833 --> 00:03:34.967
Hey, I have an idea.

00:03:34.967 --> 00:03:37.267
Say hello to the wall!

00:03:37.267 --> 00:03:38.600
[gravity gun hums]
What the hell?

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:39.733
I hit the buttons!

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:40.967
Dammit!

00:03:41.631 --> 00:03:43.633
Oh! Okay...hi!

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:45.833
Fuck it...

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:50.240
Friggin' thespians...

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.367
[explosion]
OH!

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:53.200
Wah!

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:57.800
Maybe I should've picked
another building to cut through.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:01.767
Well, I've spent so many bullets on
this one, I almost HAVE to keep going.

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:05.533
Plus, it's a breath of fresh air
shooting people that don't shoot back.

00:04:05.533 --> 00:04:07.533
That really makes all the difference.

00:04:07.533 --> 00:04:09.033
Hey, there's a thought.

00:04:09.033 --> 00:04:12.133
What if nobody ever shoots at me again?

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:15.267
That attack back there was
the last time? It's over?

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:19.967
Although, it is suspicious JUST how
quiet it got. I didn't walk that far.

00:04:19.967 --> 00:04:21.060
[distant howling]
What the hell?

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.833
VOICE: For it was said they
had become like these--

00:04:22.833 --> 00:04:23.333
What?

00:04:23.333 --> 00:04:28.100
VOICE: --peculiar demons which dwell in
matter but in whom no light may be found.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.300
Demons and matter and light...?

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:33.300
Is someone talking about the
crepuscular theory of light?

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.600
I wouldn't have expected
that in this neighborhood.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:38.567
Well, whatever. I'm not
talking to detached voices.

00:04:38.567 --> 00:04:41.600
That's a secret-of-my-success
move right there.

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:44.533
Okay, well, I appreciate the limbo challenge,

00:04:44.533 --> 00:04:48.479
but it's been a long day. I'm just
not in the mood for this anymore.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:52.933
Nope. Limbo, it is. Well, you first.

00:04:52.933 --> 00:04:54.733
I don't need to prove anything to you.

00:04:54.733 --> 00:04:56.300
Your moves are shit.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:57.631
I don't have any music.

00:04:58.247 --> 00:04:59.800
You suck!

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:02.353
What about you, scrub? You ready for this?

00:05:02.353 --> 00:05:03.200
You ready?

00:05:04.233 --> 00:05:05.377
Didn't think so.

00:05:05.377 --> 00:05:07.200
This is STREET limbo!

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:10.067
Though, if we're being honest,
we really did need some music.

00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:12.400
It probably hurt their
performance a little bit.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:17.233
It does seem awfully wasteful having these
blades spin all the time like this, though.

00:05:17.233 --> 00:05:21.333
On Eddie's property, his blade traps were
pressure-activated. Much more efficient.

00:05:21.333 --> 00:05:21.733
Nyah!

00:05:21.733 --> 00:05:22.367
VOICE: For the days of my life...

00:05:22.367 --> 00:05:24.133
AGH! What the fuck?!

00:05:24.133 --> 00:05:25.800
VOICE: ...and my bones are parched like ash,

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:26.600
What...

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:27.500
VOICE: ...and let all my impurities...

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:28.233
Shut up!

00:05:29.533 --> 00:05:30.467
I can't focus!

00:05:30.467 --> 00:05:33.067
VOICE: ...until nothing remains
but the Light alone.

00:05:33.067 --> 00:05:38.033
Yeah, I'm a physicist! Trust me. There's
nothing you know about light that I don't.

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:43.593
Eh. See, I'm breaking my own rule: Talking
back to the voice. Shouldn't do that.

00:05:45.233 --> 00:05:47.167
Oh! I didn't even see that.

00:05:47.167 --> 00:05:50.667
I should shoot it, but I kind of
want to see if go through the blade.

00:05:50.667 --> 00:05:51.500
No...

00:05:52.633 --> 00:05:55.140
Oh, it did it! I wasn't even looking.

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:58.800
Oh, new customers! All
right... All right, this way.

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:01.300
Today's special is...a wooden pallet...

00:06:01.867 --> 00:06:03.383
My name is Gordon...

00:06:04.367 --> 00:06:05.674
Can I take your order?

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:08.267
I'll get a kids' menu.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:10.233
Ah! Dammit!

00:06:10.233 --> 00:06:14.300
Fuck this! I don't need this job! I
know you weren't going to tip, either!

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:16.467
Fucking dinner shift, man...

00:06:16.467 --> 00:06:17.989
Is this how you behave at home?!

00:06:19.233 --> 00:06:20.333
I'm not cleaning this!

00:06:21.467 --> 00:06:24.433
Any more? Let's just settle the bill now!

00:06:24.433 --> 00:06:25.333
No?

00:06:25.333 --> 00:06:28.533
Well, this is still a lot more
relaxed than most of the day's been.

00:06:28.533 --> 00:06:31.433
Yeah, I don't know if I'm
going to be shot at again.

00:06:31.433 --> 00:06:32.067
Blah.

00:06:32.067 --> 00:06:34.467
I mean, storming the base
must've kept them busy,

00:06:34.467 --> 00:06:37.433
but they'll probably do a sweep
of the area if they still want me.

00:06:37.433 --> 00:06:41.600
And do they really want ME, or
was the base the real prize?

00:06:42.633 --> 00:06:45.833
The cops just sort of shoot anything
you dangle in front of them.

00:06:45.833 --> 00:06:47.400
They're almost like animals.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:49.700
Okay, do I want to go this way?

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:51.933
This looks like a yes.

00:06:51.933 --> 00:06:55.067
Y'know what? Let's save my
bullets. The night's still young.

00:06:55.067 --> 00:06:57.866
Really, it would be better if
I didn't have to kill so many,

00:06:57.866 --> 00:07:00.300
so I could save some for
the cops following me.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:04.200
But that's a tricky balance when
things are cramped and I'm lost.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:05.400
Yeah, over here.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:08.433
If you're in an abandoned town
surrounded by fifty zombies,

00:07:08.433 --> 00:07:11.333
you have to ask yourself,
"Am I going the right way?"

00:07:12.367 --> 00:07:15.733
I mean, let's get real. They're
probably torturing the rebels right now,

00:07:15.733 --> 00:07:17.600
and they'll tell them where I went.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:18.933
Though, maybe not.

00:07:18.933 --> 00:07:22.633
They could've just shot them all,
even though that'd be a stupid move.

00:07:22.633 --> 00:07:24.633
Wouldn't be their first one today.

00:07:24.633 --> 00:07:26.633
Wonder if the robot has a log.

00:07:26.633 --> 00:07:28.767
VOICE: May they become like
dust before the wind...

00:07:28.767 --> 00:07:29.725
Oh, Kansas?

00:07:29.725 --> 00:07:31.900
VOICE: ...and may the Angel
of the Lord pursue them.

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:34.367
Anyway, I just don't know
how much credit to give them.

00:07:35.203 --> 00:07:36.829
Oh, do I want to go for the trap?

00:07:37.867 --> 00:07:40.496
No, I don't. We're going
to do this the classic way.

00:07:41.547 --> 00:07:44.767
Dammit, why do zombies have to
be so pissed off all the time?

00:07:44.767 --> 00:07:46.600
Okay, I guess they have an excuse.

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:47.900
[explosion]

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:51.173
But you're not the only ones
pissed off at life, y'know.

00:07:51.173 --> 00:07:54.100
Huh, I wonder if I killed
that guy who was talking.

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:57.620
I didn't mean to, but, y'know...
You're judged by the company you keep.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:59.733
I don't like setting off explosives.

00:07:59.733 --> 00:08:01.700
Oh! Well, I like THAT.

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:03.533
Explosives are too much attention.

00:08:03.533 --> 00:08:04.300
Oh, now you...!

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:09.300
Oh come on!

00:08:10.700 --> 00:08:14.920
So, a fucking fuel barrel
exploding doesn't wake you up...

00:08:15.467 --> 00:08:16.467
NYAH!

00:08:16.467 --> 00:08:18.667
...but my footsteps, that's what does it.

00:08:18.667 --> 00:08:20.900
I just don't understand the undead.

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:25.467
Yeah, how's that saying go? "Ah,
to be young again. And a zombie."

00:08:25.467 --> 00:08:28.567
Yeah, I never got that. Maybe
I'm remembering it wrong.

00:08:29.367 --> 00:08:30.533
Okay...

00:08:31.033 --> 00:08:32.567
Shit.
[man laughing manically]

00:08:32.567 --> 00:08:33.849
Brain freeze...
[man laughing manically]

00:08:34.467 --> 00:08:35.036
You!

00:08:37.767 --> 00:08:38.449
...now you!

00:08:40.367 --> 00:08:41.560
Okay, who are YOU?!

00:08:41.967 --> 00:08:43.174
I'm kind of tired.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:44.771
Is this a concert?

00:08:44.771 --> 00:08:46.300
MAN: But, who is this?

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:46.788
Dad?

00:08:46.788 --> 00:08:48.433
MAN: Another life to save?

00:08:48.433 --> 00:08:49.733
No, he has an accent...

00:08:49.733 --> 00:08:54.133
MAN: I'll keep my eye on you.
More than that, I cannot promise.

00:08:54.133 --> 00:08:57.133
Well, you don't look like a
cop. That's all that matters.

00:08:57.133 --> 00:08:58.333
All right, bye.

00:08:58.333 --> 00:09:00.100
Man, fuck cops.

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:03.700
Yeah, I was wondering if they even
keep statistics on casualties now,

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:04.933
or just don't bother.

00:09:04.933 --> 00:09:06.600
I mean, they were probably
getting back numbers

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:09.433
showing half the police deaths
coming from friendly fire,

00:09:09.433 --> 00:09:13.500
so at that point, why bother writing
it down? It would just hurt morale.

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:17.433
Yeah, I don't like fires. Those
can be seen from the air, right?

00:09:18.733 --> 00:09:20.133
For fuck's sake!

00:09:21.767 --> 00:09:22.867
Gotta do everything...

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:25.967
Comin' out of the walls like a...

00:09:26.567 --> 00:09:27.833
...walrus...

00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:31.567
Yeah, I guess they're
not undead. Just...hosts.

00:09:31.567 --> 00:09:36.467
Oh what? They're eating them
now? I'm...I'm not there, yet.

00:09:36.467 --> 00:09:39.333
The meat's going to spoil left out like that.

00:09:39.333 --> 00:09:44.833
Okay, a valve. This is either going to
put out the fire or cause an explosion.

00:09:44.833 --> 00:09:46.267
Let's give it a turn.

00:09:48.067 --> 00:09:50.033
So this is just a propane tank.

00:09:50.033 --> 00:09:52.233
How long was he expecting this to last?

00:09:52.233 --> 00:09:54.633
Is this a holiday? I doubt it.

00:09:56.167 --> 00:09:57.100
Don't look at me!

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:59.467
AH! I SHOT IT!

00:09:59.467 --> 00:10:01.500
AHHH! WHAT THE FUCK?!

00:10:03.233 --> 00:10:07.467
Maybe I could find a motorcycle
helmet? That would be ALMOST as good.

00:10:07.467 --> 00:10:10.000
Guess I haven't seen a lot of motorcycles.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.967
It wouldn't surprise me if a
lot of bikers survived this.

00:10:12.967 --> 00:10:16.567
Run from the law, run from
aliens. Can't be that different.

00:10:16.567 --> 00:10:18.800
Okay, let's actually make this useful.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:20.321
How do I ignite it? This?

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:22.286
Yeah, that's it.

00:10:22.286 --> 00:10:24.233
[zombies yowling]

00:10:24.233 --> 00:10:25.214
Um, uh...

00:10:25.214 --> 00:10:27.567
[yowling intensifies]

00:10:27.567 --> 00:10:28.327
Uh...

00:10:30.467 --> 00:10:32.767
This isn't why I got into physics.

00:10:32.767 --> 00:10:36.267
This is the difference between
theory and practice, right here.

00:10:36.267 --> 00:10:37.567
I don't want this shit.

00:10:37.567 --> 00:10:40.500
This is why I can't talk to all
these happy-go-lucky people.

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:42.733
"How you doin', Dr. Freeman? Ahyuck!"

00:10:42.733 --> 00:10:43.833
[imitating zombie yowl]

00:10:43.833 --> 00:10:47.033
Yeah, I don't know. I think
this place is losing its charm.

00:10:47.033 --> 00:10:49.733
I mean, when I'm being
shot at from a helicopter,

00:10:49.733 --> 00:10:52.933
I think all I want in
life is for that to stop,

00:10:52.933 --> 00:10:55.533
but I guess I want more than that, too.

00:10:55.533 --> 00:10:57.933
I mean... Yeah, what's happening here?

00:10:57.933 --> 00:11:02.100
He had to have jumped up
there AND gotten stuck. Why?

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:04.633
Is this a European "Jackass" thing?

00:11:04.633 --> 00:11:09.633
"Hi, I'm Johnny Knoxville, and today we're
doing the Electric Fence Climbing Contest."

00:11:09.633 --> 00:11:12.400
Oh! Maybe they're the ones that
tried to eat the facehuggers,

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:14.100
then the whole show went to hell.

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:15.567
Well, I'm not climbing it.

00:11:15.567 --> 00:11:17.833
Oh, it's powered there? Alright...

00:11:17.833 --> 00:11:19.867
This is a real fall from grace.

00:11:19.867 --> 00:11:23.700
They needed some straightening out,
but that lab had a lot of potential.

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:28.567
I mean we had teleporters, we had
gravity control, we had a mech...

00:11:28.567 --> 00:11:30.833
Battery breakthrough, I don't know now.

00:11:30.833 --> 00:11:33.333
The gravity gun died awful fast.

00:11:33.333 --> 00:11:35.867
But any one of those is a game changer.

00:11:35.867 --> 00:11:38.733
Combined, we could hit back so hard.

00:11:38.733 --> 00:11:42.533
All we needed was production.
A factory would've done it.

00:11:42.533 --> 00:11:45.267
It's like we could win the
race if we could just stand up,

00:11:45.267 --> 00:11:47.200
but we're being kicked while we're down.

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:51.300
That feels worse than if it was
hopeless, because NOW it's hopeless.

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:54.200
It makes me think of that scene in
"An American Werewolf in London",

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:56.367
where the monsters wait and hold him hostage

00:11:56.367 --> 00:12:00.367
to watch them kill everyone
first, THEN slit his throat?

00:12:00.367 --> 00:12:02.700
That's probably what I'll
be dreaming about tonight.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:05.424
Or maybe this is electro-Jesus.

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:07.007
Maybe.

00:12:10.133 --> 00:12:14.133
I wonder if the circular saw-blade
guy went on to become a supervillain.

00:12:14.133 --> 00:12:17.526
It's a pretty good gimmick. This
is just where it all started.

